We know that $i^2 = -1,$ by definition. Therefore, [asy]
draw((0,0)--(0,3)--(3,3)--(3,0)--cycle);
draw((0,0)--(1,2));
draw((1,0)--(2,1),Arrow);
draw((2,0)--(3,2),Arrow);
draw((0,3)--(0,5));
draw((2,3)--(2,5),Arrow);
draw((1,0)--(1,1),Arrow);
draw((1,3)--(1,4),Arrow);
draw((0,3)--(2,5),Arrow);
draw((0,5)--(3,0),Arrow);
draw((1,0)--(3,3),Arrow);[/asy] It follows that $\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 3 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 5 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix} \dotsm \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 99 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}=\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 990 \\\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}}$. The answer is \begin{pmatrix}1&990\0&1\end{pmatrix}
